 clock  The specimen bears a REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm grossly unremarkable tan nipple areolar complex  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior aspect is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal diffusely fibrous parenchyma with no discrete lesions identified  Representative sections of fibrous parenchyma are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  and labeled  right axillary lymph nodes   are multiple unoriented fragments of potential lymph node bearing fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The specimen is dissected to reveal 3 lymph nodes ranging in size from 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative fibrous tissue  Received in formalin  and labeled  right breast anterior flap   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue which is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked black  bisected  and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  and labeled  right breast skin   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink skin ellipse which is excised to a depth up to 0 4cm  No lesion is grossly identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  and labeled  left breast skin   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm grossly unremarkable tan pink skin ellipse excised to a depth up to 1 2cm  focally the deep margin consists of grossly unremarkable adipose tissue   The resection margins are inked black  sectioning reveals no definitive lesion  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by David C Wilbur M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 07   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09 08 22