Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  AMY S  COLWELL  M D  Resident  Elizabeth Demicco  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 49 year old woman with a history of left breast cancer undergoing re excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  MINUTE FOCUS OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  6  SKIN WITH SCAR WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  SEE TABLE 1 AND NOTE  B  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL INFERIOR   EXCISION  1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE   0 1cm  microscopic measurement  see note  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  See prior report MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Residual invasive carcinoma is present in a minute focus measuring less than 0 1cm  Extensive DCIS is present in 5 of 8 blocks in the multiple separate foci both in association with the healing biopsy site and in other areas of the breast  A panel of immunostains including p63  calponin  myosin and cytokeratin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  confirm the presence of residual invasive carcinoma  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a 540 gram  REMOVED_DATE x 15 x 3 2cm left simple mastectomy specimen  On the anterior surface  there is a 9 x 4 5cm portion of skin  consisting of 6cm linear scar with up to 0 5cm of skin excised on either side of it  attached to a REMOVED_DATE x 3cm areolar complex  with 1 x 1 x 0 6cm nipple  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating the axillary tail  Also received in the same container are 2 portions of skin aggregating to 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm ill defined firm mass with central fat necrosis and surgical clips  located in the upper outer quadrant of the breast towards the axillary tail  The mass approaches to 0 3cm of the posterior margin  and 2 5cm of the anterior margin  The remainder of the breast is primarily fibroadipose tissue  with small areas of fibrocystic change  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nearest anterior margin radially towards mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections through mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of fibrocystic change adjacent to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of apparently unremarkable fibroadipose tissue distant from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section through scar on skin  and representative sections through also separately submitted skin in same container  Received in formalin  labeled  additional inferior tissue  left breast   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to 5 x 4 x 0 8cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 27   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 02 18PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Left Additional inferior   Excision  report_end  , Absent.
