Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 21 CLINICAL DATA  Breast mass  stitch marks new deep margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN SIZE  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN WITH LYMPHATIC AND PERINEURAL INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS  SLIDE G   BREAST  LEFT  NEW DEEP RESECTION MARGIN   EXCISION  1  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE CONSISTING OF FIBROCIS  CYSTIC CHANGES  FOCAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  2  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  3  RADIAL SCAR  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  The tumor displays some features of medullary carcinoma  focal dense lymphoid infiltrate and poorly differentiated nuclei   However  additional permanent sections display an infiltrative margin  glandular differentiation  and lack of syncitial formation which is diagnostic for a poorly differentiated carcinoma rather than a medullary carcinoma  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 39 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  MASS   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number in two parts  Labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm mass of fibroadipose tissue  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overlying skin ellipse  The deepest portion of the specimen is focally hard  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan  gritty mass that abuts the inked resection margin  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted as A  Representative portions of the tumor including the closest resection margin are submitted in B through E  A representative portion of the overlying skin is submitted in F  Representative portions of grossly unremarkable tissue is submitted in G through I  A gross photograph is taken  Labeled  new deep resection margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch marking the deepest portion  The deep margin