Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 75 year old woman with a history of invasive lobular carcinoma undergoing a right breast tissue biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION 1  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2  LYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION PRESENT   SEE NOTE  Note  Sections reveal skin and subcutis with underlying fibroadipose tissue diffusely infiltrated by carcinoma  The submitted specimen was not oriented and margins cannot be assessed  however the tumor is present in multiple discrete foci throughout the specimen and grows in cords and trabeculae with a distinctly single file pattern characteristic of invasive lobular carcinoma  The tumor cells are small to intermediate in size with rare cytoplasmic vacuoles and have eccentrically placed nuclei with subtle nuclear contour irregularities  The tumor extends to the level of the epidermis and involvement of the dermal lymphatics is present  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan to pink fibrous soft tissue with sparse attached adipose tissue and a separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm lobulated yellow fatty tissue surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm unremarkable tan skin ellipse  No orienting tissues are present  The smaller tissue is serially sectioned to reveal white tan fibrous tissue and is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The larger tissue is serially sectioned to reveal lobulated yellow adipose tissue and is submitted in its entirety as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Right   Excision  report_end  , Absent.
