5cm from the posterior surface and 1cm from the anterior surface and corresponds to the overlying scar at 10 o clock position  A hemorrhagic tract which measures 4 5cm in length is present beneath the second scar and abuts the cavity and the overlying posterior surface  Small foci of orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis is present in and around the cavity and along the hemorrhagic linear tract  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows diffuse fibrous thickening with focal cystic change  No lymph nodes are identified in the axillary portion  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections from the biopsy  including closest to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections from the hemorrhagic linear tract  including closest to the posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section from the breast parenchyma where the cavity and the tract abut each other   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma away from the cavity  upper inner quadrant Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Absent.
