 REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm and shows nipple and areola which also appear unremarkable  The anterior  margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen  contains an irregularly outlined  tan pink to gray white  firm  focally  necrotic lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  in the upper quadrants   predominantly in the upper outer quadrant and 0 5cm from the nearest anterior  margin and 0 5cm from the nearest posterior margin  The breast parenchyma  adjacent to this lesion shows dense pink white fibrosis  The remaining breast  parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and pink white fibrous stroma  An  obvious tumor or a metallic clip are not identified  No lymph nodes are  identified in the lateral portion of the specimen  Representative sections are  submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   Cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lesion in the upper quadrant   cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the most medial portion of the lesion  cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representing the entire lesion adjacent to the section in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  extending from superior to inferior  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the most inferior  portion of the lesion  and cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the lateral aspect of  the lesion  from superior to inferior  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the most  inferior portion of the lesion   Cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma with diffuse fibrosis  medial to the  lesion   Cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma away from the lesion and showing minimal  fibrosis   Cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral aspect of the specimen  without lymph nodes   Cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of the 4 4cm lesion     Received fresh  and labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm   mastectomy specimen with a short suture designa