Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 26 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  99    REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED MARGIN   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Microcalcifications are associated with the invasive carcinoma  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  3  SEVERELY ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA PRESENT AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND AT AN INKED SURFACE  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 13                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  with a specimen x ray and needle locallizing wire in place in a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm mass of lobated breast tissue  A white firm stellate nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm is 0 6cm from the nearest inked margin and is grossly suspicious for carcinoma  No frozen done  Entirely in A through D  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Present.
