esions are identified and are described below in a medial to lateral fashion  Lesion  1  most medial  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and extends 1 8cm of the deep margin and 1 7cm of the anterior superior margin  Lesion  2  medial  is located 1cm lateral to lesion  1 and is ill defined mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The lesion extends to 3 5cm of the deep margin and 0 3cm of the anterior superior margin  Lesion  3  central  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and is located in the superior central portion of the breast and extends to 3 8cm of the deep margin to approximately 2cm of the anterior margin  The lesion is located approximately 6cm lateral to lesion  2  Lesion  2 3 have blue dye adjacent to them  Lesion  4 is  most lateral  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and is located 2 0cm from the deep margin and 4 3cm from the anterior margin  The 4th lesion is located approximately 4 5cm lateral to the largest lesion   lesion  3   The remainder of the tissue consists predominately of adipose tissue with a few foci of soft white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  B D  Lesion  1  E G  Lesion  2  H I  Lesion  3  J  Shave margin  deep margin beneath lesion  3  K L  Lesion  4  M N  Sections of fibrous tissue between the different lesions  Gross Description by  TIM J  ROBINSON Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  BIOPSY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Absent.
