Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 52 CLINICAL DATA  77 year old female with breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE WITH NECROSIS AND LUMINAL MICROCALCIFICATION  PRESENT IN ONE OF NINE BLOCKS  SEE NOTE  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  BIOPSY SITES  2  WITH FIBROSIS  HEMORRHAGE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND GIANT CELL REACTION  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH MICROCYSTS  FIBROSIS  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND MICROCALCIFICATION  NOTE  STROMAL  BLOOD VASCULAR AND LYMPHATIC INVASION IS NOT IDENTIFIED  LYMPH NODES RIGHT AXILLA  AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWELVE OF TWELVE LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 37                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in a container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a right modified radical mastectomy with a left breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and overlying skin ellipse  which measures REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm with accompanying nipple and areolar and an axillary tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  Approximately 3 0cm lateral to the nipple is a recent surgical incision  closed by suture  measures 3 0cm  Approximately 4 0cm medially and superiorly is a second recent surgical incision closed with suture  measuring 4 0cm in length  Immediately below the medial surgical scar is a firm stellate  yellowish tan  lesion with areas of hemorrhage measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The lesion is approximately 1 0cm from the deepest closest resection margin  Immediately adjacent to the lateral surgical scar is an ill defined  yellowish tan  stellate lesion  measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  There are focal areas of hemorrhage within this lesion and the lesion is approximately 1 0cm from the closest resection margin  In the remaining parenchyma are multiple small nodules in the upper outer quadrant  each measuring approximately 0 5cm in greatest dimension  The axillary tissue is examined for lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  AandB  representative sections of the lesion  immediately adjacent to the medial scar with representative skin C DandE  representative sections of the medial lesion with representative sections of the deep resection margin F  representative section of the lesion adjacent to the lateral scar with skin and lateral resection margin G  representative section of the lateral lesion  with deep resection margin H  representative section of the lateral lesion I  representative section of the nodular areas J  representative sections of five possible lymph nodes  the largest measuring 0 5cm in greatest dimension K  representative section of five possible lymph nodes  the largest measuring 0 6cm in greatest dimension L  representative sections of two possible lymph nodes  the largest measuring 1 0cm in greatest dimension  Resident  KEITH KWAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Present.
