d  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL NODE COUNT 135    EXCISION  FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS  SEE NOTE   NOTE  A tiny cluster of keratin positive tumor cells is identified on one of three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels only  The cells are at the edge of the lymph node where the tissue is disrupted making the interpretation difficult  Dr  Melinda Lerwill reviewed the slide and concurs  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL NODE COUNT 75    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled with  right sentinel node  135   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink lymph node  with minimally attached tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled with  right sentinel node  75   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink lymph node  which is trisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled with  right breast  stitch axillary tail   is a 713 gram  19 x 15 x 2 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch on the axillary tail  The anterior surface contains a 6 x 4cm tan brown skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areola and 1 x 1 x 0 5cm nipple  which are both grossly unremarkable  There is a 2cm linear well healed scar present approximately at 7 o clock  1cm from the areola  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  and posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 3cm tan white  ill defined fibrotic healing biopsy site  which is present approximately between the 6 and 7 o clock positions  and which abuts the posterior inked margin and lies beneath the well healed linear skin scar  The metallic clip is grossly appreciated  The remaining breast parenchyma contains tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with scant amount of tan white fibrous tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly appreciated in the upper outer quadrant tissue  where the axillary tail stitch is located  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the biopsy site  including the closest posterior and anterior inked margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma at the level of the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma at the level of the inner lower quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast skin margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of fragmented tan white skin  which is inked black and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the t