ht green discoloration  It is 1 8cm from the nearest posterior resection margin  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the medial most stellate lesion including the anterior and the posterior resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the solid area lateral to the first stellate lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the second stellate lesion including a section towards the nearest posterior resection margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of the ill defined cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section of the breast away from the lesions  The axillary tail is dissected from lymph nodes and potential lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One potential lymph nodes  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  RIGHT   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  SEVERAL SMALL FOCI   1 MM   IN ONE NODE AND A SUBCAPSULAR FOCUS APPROXIMATELY 3 MM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN A SECOND NODE  MORE TUMOR IS SEEN ON THE DEEPER SECTIONS THAN ON FIRST SECTION   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART C  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY  , Absent.
