Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Aleksandr Vasilyev  M D  Reports To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left modified radical mastectomy  invasive ductal carcinoma    FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm  Grade  3  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Suspicious  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Positive at the deep margin of the specimen in one focus and present less than 0 05cm from the deep margin along a broad front  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS 2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  13 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   1 Extracapsular extension  Marked  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm left radical mastectomy specimen with a stitch indicating 12 o clock  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse attached to the specimen  Areola and the subareolar tissue completely excised  The skin around the excision site is focally ulcerated and nodular  The skin ellipse occupies the entire anterior surface of the specimen  therefore the anterior surface is not inked  The posterior is inked black  the superior is inked green and the inferior is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm hard  leathery  tan light brown mass in the subareolar area  The center of the mass corresponds to the biopsy site  which is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The mass appears to abut the posterior resection margin  it is roughly 5 0cm from the inferior resection margin  6 0cm from the superior margin and focally extends to the skin surface but does not appear to involve the skin resection margins  Four representative sections of the lesion with the posterior resection margin are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved breast with the inferior resection margin closest to the lesion is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the uninvolved breast with superior margin closest to lesion submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The attached axillary tissue was dissected for lymph nodes  Several potential lymph nodes were identified and submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node quadrisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes  Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for pr