Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  RAD Mammography Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  RACHEL ANN HITT  M D  CONNIE ROCHE  NP Resident  Russell Ryan  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 59 year old woman with two left breast mass lesions  Lesion  1  specimen  A   is a BIRADS 5 on mammogram and U S and is located at 4 00 o clock  Lesion  2  specimen  B   is a 3 to 4cm heterogeneous mass on U S at 1 o clock  possibly a fibroadenoma  located at 1 00 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  see note   NOTE  The tumor is composed of large cells with abundant cytoplasm and fairly low nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio  The nuclei have irregular contours and hyperchromatic vesicular chromatin with prominent nucleoli  To confirm the diagnosis  we performed a panel of immunostains with the following results  STAIN TARGET RESULT E cadherin Ductal differentiation Positive Cytokeratin Epithelial cells Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive CDX 2 GI epithelium Negative  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Macrophages Negative TTF 1 Lung Thyroid Negative Vimentin Renal cell CA Negative The immunoperoxidase staining pattern supports the morphologic findings and overall  the findings are compatible with invasive ductal carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT  1 00   CORE BIOPSY  2  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH HYALINIZED STROMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  see note   NOTE  The findings may not correlate with the clinical impression of a mass lesion  Clinical correlation to ensure adequate sampling of the targeted lesion is suggested  Multiple levels were examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  1 of 2  4 o clock   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  breast 1 o clock  2 of 2   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  1 PART B  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  2  report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 24 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable nodules at 3 o clock on the right  calcium at 12 o clock on the right      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  AMENDED CLINICAL HISTORY Revised by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Revised on 10 AUG 98 at 11 47                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  TISSUE CALCIFICATIONS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  TWO SEPARATE FOCI SPANNING REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY PRESENT AT INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT  BREAST NODULE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCALLY PRESENT AT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE CLOSEST RESECTION MARGIN  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Edited by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 16 10 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   Tissue calcifications    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast tissue calcification  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm unoriented fibroadipose breast tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma  submitted entirely in A through F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 6cm fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in G and H  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST NODULE   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  TISSUE CALCIFICATIONS    EXCISIONAL PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  BREAST NODULE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
