or protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary sentinel lymph node  are three pieces of fatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 3cm  One is entirely frozen as FX 1 and the other two remaining are entirely frozen as FX 2  now as A and B respectively  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of breast with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink skin  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon with a long suture designating lateral  and a short suture designating superior  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined area of dense gritty fibrous tissue  extending to the posterior inferior and superior margins  The remaining breast tissue is unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked black and the posterior margin overinked red and the superior margin is overinked yellow  The specimen is entirely submitted from lateral to medial in cassette C O  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final inferior medial margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  Representative sections are submitted in cassette P through S 