Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT    LOWER LESION   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT    UPPER LESION   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 23                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   LOWER LESION     THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   UPPER LESION    THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Right breast lower lesion   are 3 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 1 0cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Right breast  upper lesion   are 4 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE X 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as B  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST   LOWER LESION   CORE BIOPSY PART B  RIGHT BREAST   UPPER LESION   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
