Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 27 CLINICAL DATA    inflammatory carcinoma of right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  SUBMITTED FRESH   BIOPSY  ADENOCARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  INFILTRATING  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED   SEE NOTE   BREAST  RIGHT  SUBMITTED IN FORMALIN   BIOPSY  ADENOCARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  INFILTRATING  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is consistent with ductal carcinoma and is present within numerous vessels  The vessels contain virtually no blood cells  making them consistent with lymphatics rather than veins  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of breast tissue  The specimen is bisected to reveal fibrous tissue  half frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen for Cox 5  The remainder is submitted in A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  which has been partially incised by the surgeon  The specimen is submitted entirely in B  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MASS PART B  RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Absent.
