gy  None   Office Notes  REMOVED_DATE   K  Elliott  NP     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  protocol  Examination of the left breast and chest wall reveals an ill defined  firm fixed 2cm mass   11 00  10cm from the areola  Both nipples inverted     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  consent was obtained  4 aspirates were performed using 23 gauge needles with  local anesthesia and without complications  2 slides were stained for immediate  evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to NP K  Elliott by phone at  3 o clock p m          Electronically Signed Out By  Elena Brachtel  M D  on REMOVED_DATE 17 36       CLINICAL HISTORY    Self palpated left breast mass   11 00  Reports history of trauma in REMOVED_MONTH   REMOVED_CASE_ID   thick book fell from shelf and hit her on the chest          SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 2 slides in ETOH and 2 rapid slides     B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  name and  medical number   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a collodion bag  Entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  casette           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Specimen  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT       report_end  , Absent.
