s reveals yellow fatty tissue with diffuse white and firm areas with no grossly identifiable mass  There is a smooth REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm partial cavity which abuts the inferior and medial margins  is 1 5cm from the lateral margin   1 0cm from both the anterior and posterior margin and  1 0cm from the superior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior margin  representative section taken radially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin taken en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of white firm area to closest margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of cavity to nearest margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of white firm area to closest margins  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  new inferior margin   is a yellow red REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm portion of breast tissue with a bowtie designating the new margin and short ties encircling the inferior surgical bed which is all inked in black  At the surgical bed  there is a smooth lined red REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm partially opened cavity which abuts the margins  Serial sectioning reveals a cavity extending the length of the entire specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm bulge into the cavity which is located 1 0cm from the closest margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma has diffuse yellow discoloration around the biopsy cavity  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior sections of the biopsy cavity site designated by the short stitches taken en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of inferior portion of specimen taken radially to the nearest margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial section of bulge into the cavity taken radially to the nearest margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of biopsy cavity to nearest margin  Gross Dictation by Adam J Saenz M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Adam J Saenz M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Significant additional diagnostic information gained from additional tissue processed  Note  According to the surgeon  specimen  A   Left breast  is a separate excisional biopsy for mammographic calcifications in the upper outer quadrant  although in the vicinity of the prior excisional biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Additional tissue sections were submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   to ensure the calcifications were adequately sampled  Significantly  two microscopic foci of invasive tubulo lobular carcinoma were identified  grade 1 of 3  spanning 0 15cm and 0 2cm  These foci are identified in 2 separate tissue sections  and may or may not be contiguous  They are   0 2cm from the margin  One of the foci is present within a few millimeters of healing biopsy changes  There is no evidence of angiolymphatic invasion  The majority of calcifications are associated with fibrocystic changes  although calcifications are also seen associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia and the initially reported focus of ductal carcinoma in situ  The latter is low grade  and not associated with the prior healing biopsy site  Additional sections were also submitted on specimen  B   Left breast  new inferior margin     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   revealing a few additional foci of grade 2 ductal carcinoma in situ    0 2cm from the margin  The DCIS cells stain positive with E cadherin  Results of immunostains for myoepithelial markers  p63 and calponin  help to exclude invasion in this specimen in a focus of lobular cancerization  Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT NEW INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION , Present.
