Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 15 08 CLINICAL DATA  63 year old female with large  ulcerating mass  left breast  family history of breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The entire specimen consists of invasive carcinoma which extends to the inked resection margins  Lymphatic invasion is present  There is no evidence of an in situ component  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Cooper  MD Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 13 24                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 324 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 611 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 14 56     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 16 56     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 MAY 97 at 15 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab in two parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  Perm   is a 3 x 2 x 2cm  grossly firm  white tissue with infiltrating borders  No frozen slides  The frozen tissue is saved for cytogenetics  Tissue is submtted for estrogen receptors and BRDU  Labeled  Left breast tissue  are three fragments of fibrofatty tissue  measuring in aggregate 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  The entire breast tissue from both specimens is submitted in cassettes A through F  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  ELLISON 08 REPORTS TO  Jo Buyske  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Absent.
