e performed using 25 gauge needles  without anesthesia and without complications  1 slide was stained for immediate  evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Ultrasound was used for evaluation of the lesion     Ultrasound Findings  Small hypoechoic lesion     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Dr  Gadd in person at 4  o clock P M       The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Joseph Misdraji MD on REMOVED_DATE 18 20       CLINICAL HISTORY  Left breast lump noted by patient         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 4 slides in ETOH           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT       report_end  , Absent.
