Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 AUG 98 at 15 18 CLINICAL DATA  Irregular speculated mass suspect malignancy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH ENDOCRINE FEATURES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 AUG 98 at 15 53                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and with no designation as to site  are six cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as A  Gross Description by  Robert F Donnell Resident  QUN DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Debra Monticciolo MD Susan E Briggs  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  CORE BIOPSIES , Absent.
