tration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm axillary tail  and a REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm skin ellipse containing a 1 5cm nipple  A short stitch on the skin ellipse marks superior and a long stitch lateral  as designated by the surgeon  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a centrally located  ill defined fibrous area  approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  A distinct mass lesion is not identified  The remainder of the breast tissue consists of lobular adipose tissue with thin fibrous bands  The posterior margin appears grossly unremarkable throughout the specimen  The axillary tail contains multiple lymph nodes and soft tissue nodules measuring REMOVED_DATE to approximately 2 0cm in greatest dimension  many of these contain a waxy yellow homogeneous substance  Multiple matted lymph nodes nodules are present which cannot be individually dissected  Section code  A J  representative sections of fibrous area suspicious for tumor  K L  representative sections of posterior margin  central portion of specimen  M  representative section of skin  N Q  single lymph nodes nodules  R S  one bisected lymph node nodule each cassette  T Y  representative sections of matted lymph nodes nodules  Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 AUG 96 ACCESSIONED ON  12 AUG 96 at 09 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   NIPPLE DUCT EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  TWO MICROSCOPIC FOCI  REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The invasive carcinoma stains for keratin  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  carcinoma is not present on the frozen section slide  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT IN SIX OF SEVEN SLIDES   WITH PAYETOID SPREAD AND CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  3  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  4  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  5  FIBROADENOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 96 at 15 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 96 at 09 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of breast  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of firm white  poorly circumscribed mass surrounding the 0 4cm central duct  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in cassette A  Remainder submitted in B   G  from superficial to deep  distal end   The superficial end  short stitch  in B and the distal end  long stitch  in G  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST   INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Garth Rees Cosgrove  M D  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   NIPPLE DUCT EXCISION  RIGHT    report_end  , Present.
