Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  24 MAY 96 at 13 09 CLINICAL DATA  71 year old woman with left breast infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN FOUR OF TWENTY LYMPH NODES  WITH EXTRANODAL EXTENTION IN ONE LYMPH NODE AND PERINODAL LYMPHATIC INVOLVEMENT IN ONE LYMPH NODE  2  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SEVERAL FOCI ADJACENT TO HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY   SEE NOTE   3  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL LACTATIONAL CHANGE  6  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  Margins appear free of carcinoma  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL I   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 MAY 96 at 14 39                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  and unit number are two containers  Labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen including a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail  A REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm skin ellipse contains a centrally located 3 5cm unremarkable areola with an unremarkable 1 0cm in greatest dimension nipple in its center  Infero lateral to the nipple complex  is a 4 0cm healing oblique surgical incision which comes within 1 2cm of the inferior skin ellipse resection margin  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm blood and filled biopsy cavity with sutures located 2 0cm from the nearest  deep and inferior  resection margins  Tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity is tan white and semi firm to firm  The remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable with no areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma  Section code  A  biopsy cavity in relation to inked deep resection margin B  biopsy cavity in relation to inked inferior resection margin C F  representative sections of biopsy cavity G  representative section of semi firm breast tissue from medial portion of breast H  representative section of prior surgical incision I  representative section of nipple Dissection of the REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm attached axillary tail reveals numerous soft tan to semi firm lymph nodes measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest dimension  submitted in J M  Labeled  Level 1 node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm massive fatty tissue containing a single 1 0cm tan semi firm lymph node  bissected and submitted entirely in N  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  David L Berger  M D  PART A  LEVEL 1 NODE PART B  LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Present.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 59 CLINICAL DATA  Breast and nipple biopsy    Paget s disease                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN IN SEVERAL AREAS  AND FOCALLY INTO THE DERMIS OF THE OVERLYING SKIN  LYMPHATIC INVASION IS IDENTIFIED  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5   NOTE  Paget s disease is not seen  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 54                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   13  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 57     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 31     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue and overlying skin with schirrous retraction  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1cm white infiltrating lesion abutting the skin surface  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1 which is kept frozen  BRDU sent  Frozen section sent for ER and PR analysis  Remainder is submitted in cassettes A through D  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Absent.
