ENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three specimens  Labelled  left modified radical mastectomy   is a mastectomy specimen with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  On the skin ellipse there is also a 2 9cm long vertical well healed scar  The areola on the skin ellipse measures 2 9cm in diameter and has a nipple in the center with 1 2cm diameter  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity located below the well healed scar  The cavity is 0 5cm from the closest posterior resection margin  Around the biopsy cavity is relatively firm white yellow fibrous tissue  The inferior to the cavity there is a well circumscribed white 3 5cm in greatest diameter firm nodule  which is 0 2cm from the posterior  deep  margin  The remaining breast parenchyma appears grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are taken  Submitted in cassette A G  Section code  A  Biopsy cavity and nodule in relation to closest  deep  resection margin  B  Nodule C E  Biopsy cavity with adjacent nodule in relation to resection margin  F  Nodule G  Unremarkable breast parenchyma  representative section  In the axillary tail a suture designates the axillary nodes and in this area two lymph nodes are found  One lymph node measure 1 3cm in greatest diameter  the other 1 6cm in greatest diameter  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes H I  Additionally  two lymph nodes were also found in the axillary tail and are submitted in cassette J  Labelled  right modified radical mastectomy   is a mastectomy specimen with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin  On the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse which has a 2 5cm in diameter areola centered by a 1 3cm nipple  A vertical scar measuring 2 3cm in length  well healed  is located at the supra lateral portion of the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity with an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm gritty nodule is superior to the biopsy cavity  The biopsy cavity is 0 4cm from the anterior superior inked margin  The biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm and is 0 3cm from the deep margin  about 3cm inferior to the biopsy cavity there is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white firm ill defined mas