Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 09 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma on a needle aspirate                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GROSS MEASUREMENT   GRADE 3  NOTE  The tumor has abundant comedo type necrosis and sheets of pleomorphic tumors cells with no lumen formation  between dense fibrous septae  Although an entirely invasive counterpart to comedocarcinoma is the favored interpretation of this uncommon appearance  a metastatic tumor is a lesser consideration  Frozen sections of the  deep  and  superficial  aspects of the excision show tumor focally abutting margins  The tumor is well demarcated grossly and microscopically  however  and mostly has a  pushing  border rather than an irregularly infiltrating one  The additional negative margins thus may indicate that the mass is completely excised  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  No in situ component is present  SOFT TISSUE  BREAST   EXCISION OF ADDITIONAL  POSTERIOR  MARGIN  SKELETAL MUSCLE AND ADIPOSE TISSUE WITH SUTURE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  EXCISION OF ADDITIONAL  ANTERIOR  INFERIOR  MARGIN  MINOR FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SOFT TISSUE  BREAST   EXCISION OF ADDITIONAL  ANTERIOR  SUPERIOR  MARGIN  ADIPOSE TISSUE WITH SKELETAL MUSCLE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 29 of 29 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 21 56 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  and  right axillary dissection and lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with stitch  pin  marking the apex  The specimen in inked and sectioned to reveal centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm stellate firm  white mass  grossly abutting the deep margin less than 0 1cm from the superficial margin  The deep margin is frozen as FX  1  the superficial margin is frozen as FX  2 and both are resubmitted in A and B  respectively  The mass comes to within 5 0cm of the lateral margin  6 0cm of the medial margin  and 1 7cm of both the superior and inferior margin  The axillary contents are dissected for nodes  C K  lymph nodes L  section through uninvolved breast parenchyma near pin M  section through tumor N  radial section near long suture Further labeled  posterior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of muscle and fat with a black suture designating superficial margin  The suture is noted to be attached to a small portion of tissue that appears to be holding two almost completely separate pieces of muscle together  each piece accounting for approximately half of the total volume of specimen submitted  The specimen in inked in black and double inked in blue along the superficial margin indicated by suture material  O  radial section through tissue immediately beneath the suture material P  additional radial sections lateral to suture material Labeled  anterior margin  inferior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm portion of breast tissue with a black suture designating the inferior superficial margin  The specimen is inked in black and the superficial aspect opposite to the suture is double inked in blue  Q R  radial sections through the superior aspect of the specimen from lateral to medial Labeled  anterior margin  superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of breast tissue with a black suture designating the superior aspect  The specimen is very fragmented  It is inked in black entirely and the superficial aspect is inked in blue  S T  radial sections through inferior aspect  without suture  Labeled  skin around incision  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with a central portion cut open  incised to a depth of approximately 1 0cm  The defect in the center of the ellipse separates the specimen into two pieces with a skimpy portion of skin less than 0 5cm on each lateral aspect holding the two pieces together  The deep aspect of the specimen is inked in black  U  radial sections from within the opening in the skin from the portion with the short suture V  sections from the inner aspect of the tissue on the  section without the suture   Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  DEEP MARGIN   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TUMOR PRESENT AT MARGINS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST  SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TUMOR PRESENT AT MARGINS  O R  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  Deborah Jean Wald  M D  PART A  AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B  LUMPECTOMY TISSUE BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Absent.
