Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 MAY 95 at 16 05 CLINICAL DATA  46 year old female with right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 7 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT A FRACTION OF A MM FROM AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  MICROCYSTS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No ductal carcinoma in situ is identified  AXILLA  RIGHT   RESECTION  CARCINOMA METASTATIC TO 3 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  3 16   Diagnosis by  Jeoffry Brennick  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 47 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate specimens   Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm unoriented breast excision specimen  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan  firm  somewhat well defined mass  extending to less than 1mm from an inked resection margin  Representative sections in A D  Next to the periphery of the lesion is a tan  soft  ill defined area which extends to the inked margin  representative section in E   Right axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary lymph node dissection containing multiple nodules  REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest diameter  representative sections in F J  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLA  RIGHT    report_end  , Present.
