Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Preliminary Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 53 CLINICAL DATA  Please assay for estrogen and progesterone receptors                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     SKIN OF BREAST  RIGHT   INCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  TUMOR TRANSECTED   GRADE 1  INVOLVING DEEP MARGINS ACROSS BROAD FRONTS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor immunostains will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 18 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast tissue  is a firm  tan pink fragment of tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  submitted entirely in A  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Gerald Joseph Doyle  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Catherine J Wu  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   INCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
