Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 42 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 2 3   10  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  90  WITH EXTENSIVE PAGETOID SPREAD AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO INKED SURGICAL MARGIN AND APPROACHING MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No lymphatic invasion is identified  The carcinoma in situ is primarily of comedo and cribriform types  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 31 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   Neither the invasive nor the in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The invasive tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  but the in situ cells show staining for the protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue with localizing wire and accompanying x ray showing a focus of microcalcifications  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined 1 5cm area of white tissue containing scattered cysts  admixed with foci of fleshy pink tan tissue  The lesion is submitted in cassette A through C  and the remainder of the specimen in cassettes D through H  No frozen section is done  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Present.
