Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Vikram Deshpande  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Ricard Masia  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Multifocal left breast cancer  Invasive carcinoma  DCIS in separate sites  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INNER QUADRANT  9 O CLOCK   SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  UPPER INNER QUADRANT  11 O CLOCK   SEE NOTE AND TABLE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 2  WITH FOCAL NECROSIS AND CALCIFICATIONS  FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   COMPLEX SCLEROSING LESION  UPPER OUTER QUADRANT  2 O CLOCK   PARTLY INVOLVED BY DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  THREE HEALING BIOPSY SITES  2  9 AND 11 O CLOCK   NOTE  Three separate abnormal regions are identified on gross examination  and each of these is associated with a biopsy clip  One contains an invasive ductal carcinoma  with adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ   another an invasive lobular carcinoma  with adjacent lobular carcinoma in situ   and the third a complex sclerosing lesion that is partly involved by ductal carcinoma in situ and flat epithelial atypia  No definite stromal invasion is identified in the complex sclerosing lesion  using immunoperoxidase stains for markers of epithelial and myoepithelial differentiation  cytokeratin cocktail  calponin  myosin  p63   but acellular stromal mucin is seen focally adjacent to it  The invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma cells are negative for e cadherin  by immunoperoxidase methods  Fibrocystic changes with sclerosing adenosis are adjacent to all three regions  The margins are negative for invasive and in situ carcinoma of both types  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  9 0 CLOCK  TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  gross measurement  GRADE  2 LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the 9 o clock mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2 MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  11 0 CLOCK  TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x 0 35cm  measured from slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   GRADE  2 LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Not identified adjacent to invasive lobular carcinoma mass  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  No cytokeratin positive tumor cells are identified on levels immunostained for pan keratin  cytokeratin cocktail  and cytokeratin 7  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of tan pink fibrofatty tissue  which is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node  The lymph node is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen  which is partially surfaced by a 2 8cm in diameter unremarkable areola  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unremarkable  everted nipple  The specimen is received with a short suture designating the superior aspect and a long suture designating the lateral aspect  as per the surgeon  The specimen is inked for orientation as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  stellate mass within the lower outer quadrant at approximately the 9 o clock aspect of the specimen  located 1 7cm from the black inked posterior margin and 1 9cm from the anterior margin  A metallic clip is identified within this mass  Further sectioning reveals an additional metallic clip within the upper inner quadrant at approximately the 11 o clock aspect of the specimen  6 5cm from the first mass  3 0cm from the posterior margin  and 2 2cm from the anterior margin  There is focally gritty  dense gray white fibrous tissue at the periphery of this clip  however  there is no additional discrete mass identified  Further sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm gray white  slightly firm rubbery area within the upper outer quadrant at approximately the 2 o clock aspect of the specimen  2 2cm from the posterior margin and 3 6cm from the anterior margin  The remaining cut surfaces consist of predominantly dense gray white  rubbery fibrous tissue occupying approximately 40  of the cut surfaces  No additional discrete masses or lesions are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   9 o clock clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of 9 o clock mass  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is 1 section  cut in half    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   11 o clock clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative fibrous tissue at periphery of 11 o clock clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin nearest to 11 o clock clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 o clock slightly firm area  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative central fibrous tissue  Received in formalin  labeled  breast skin   are 3 fragments of fibrofatty soft tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  the largest of which is partially surfaced by tan  wrinkled tissue  possibly consistent with skin  The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 16   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 11 01AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cel