Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  RANGING IN SIZE FROM REMOVED_DATE 3 CM  EXTENSIVE   PRESENT IN EIGHT OF TEN SLIDES   WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  SOME OF WHICH ARE ALONG A BROAD FRONT  AND WITH FOCI HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT IN ALL 10 SLIDES  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  AND EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE MARGINS ALONG A BROAD FRONT  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of breast tissue with localization needle and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal lumpy  firm to rubbery  white and off yellow breast tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through J  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Absent.
