ep margin  1 5cm from the closest superior inked border  and 3 0cm deep to the overlying skin  A second biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm is located 3 0cm inferior to the first biopsy cavity  2 5cm from the closest deep inked margin  and 4 0cm deep to the overlying skin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavities is remarkable for areas of fat necrosis  white fibrous tissue  and more ill defined firm  focally gritty tissue that comes to within 4 5cm of the closest deep margin  2 5cm deep to the overlying skin and to within 2 5cm of the closest anterior inked resection margin  Approximately 1 0cm deep to the more superiorly located scar is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ill defined  firm area which comes to within 1 0cm of the closest superior inked margin and 2 0cm from the closest deep inked margin  No other discrete lesion is identified inferior to the scar  Approximately 1 5cm deep to the more inferiorly located scar is an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm area with central hemorrhage  5 5cm from the deep inked margin  and 2 5cm from the closest inferior inked resection margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma away from the biopsy cavities is composed of fibrofatty tissue  Sectioning through the axillary tail reveals multiple tan lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 3cm to 1 5cm  is identified  Also submitted with the specimen is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal multiple tan lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  A D  Representative sections of more superiorly located biopsy cavity  E   Closest inked deep margin  to the first biopsy cavity   F I  Representative sections of the more inferiorly located biopsy cavity  J   Closest inked deep margin  in relation to second biopsy cavity   K N  Representative sections of more fibrous  firm  gritty areas adjacent to biopsy cavities  O   More ill defined  firm area inferior to the superiorly located scar  P   More