Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTI  ATED  EXTENDING TO SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  AND WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  Invasive carcinoma is present throughout the entire specimen  the tumor is at least 1 5cm since the smallest specimen dimension is 1 5cm  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASION COMPONENT AND LESS THAN 1 HPF FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  DERMAL LYMPHATIC INVASION IS NOT SEEN  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  05 AUG 97 at 16 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 14 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled  Skin  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm longitudinal portion of skin excised to a depth of 0 3cm  No discrete lesions are noted on the surface  The specimen is trisected and submitted entirely in cassette A  Labeled  Breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm white stellate nodule  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1 and resubmitted in cassette K  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in cassttes B   F  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes H   J  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
