Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 57 CLINICAL DATA  Status post excision REMOVED_DATE  with confirmation of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM CLOSEST DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2 INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID TYPE  SCANT  3 METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 16 OF 27 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not identified  Ten of sixteen lymph nodes with metastatic carcinoma demonstrated extranodal extension  4 HEALING BIOPSY SITE WITH METAPLASTIC BONE FORMATION  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of stain