Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 29 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT POSTERIOR LESION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED SURGICAL MARGINS WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION IDENTIFIED  BREAST  RIGHT ANTERIOR LESION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED SURGICAL MARGINS WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION IDENTIFIED  NOTE  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  James F  XxSouthern Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 49 Proofread by  XXSOUTHERN JAMES F                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  ANTERIOR AND POSTERIOR SPECIMENS   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 28     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen consists of two parts  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast posterior lesion  is a piece fibroadipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm with a localizing wire and accompanying X ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white firm area 0 2cm from nearest inked margin  Firm area is submitted in cassettes A through C  the rest in D and E  No frozen section is done  Also received fresh in frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast anterior lesion  is a 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying X ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm white firm area extending to an inked margin  Representative sections is frozen as frozen section  1  This material is saved frozen  The firm area is submitted in cassettes F through K  the rest in cassettes L through X  No tissue was sent for estrogen or progesterone receptors or kinetic studies  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST POSTERIOR LESION   SUSPICIOUS AREA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  William H  Yong  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT POSTERIOR LESION  PART B  BREAST  RIGHT ANTERIOR LESION    report_end  , Absent.
