Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 49 CLINICAL DATA  2 separate primary tumors and positive sentinel node                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  A SINGLE REMOVED_DATE CM MICROSCOPIC FOCUS ADJACENT TO HEALING BIOPSY SITE  FAR AWAY FROM MARGINS   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  A benign nest of nevus cells is present in a lymph node capsule  BREAST  LEFT  TISSUE    EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  Diagnosis by  SELIM NASSER  MD Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 29                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  only  is a 18 x 15 x 5 0cm right modified mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  The specimen is partially surfaced by REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm skin with an eccentrically located  1cm in diameter unremarkable nipple  a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating superior  There are two 4 0cm healed linear scars present on the skin surface  one present 0 2cm from the lateral skin resection margin  the other present 0 5cm from the medial skin resection margin  The specimen is black inked and sectioned to reveal 2 separate biopsy cavity  one underlying the lateral skin scar and the other underlying the medial skin scar  The lateral cavity measures 4 0cm in largest dimension and is surrounded by tan white to yellow  firm  stellate tissue which extends to 2 0cm from its closest posterior resection margin  2 0cm from its lateral resection margin and 0 3cm from its closest anterior non skin covered resection margin  The anterior margin is inked in green  the lateral inked in blue and the medial inked in orange   The medial cavity also measures 4 0cm in largest dimension  is also surrounded by tan white yellow  firm  stellate tissue which is focally extends to the posterior resection margin  0 8cm from the closest anterior resection margin  and 2 0cm from its closest medial resection margin  Both cavities including the surrounding firm tissue are  5 0cm away from both the superior and inferior soft tissue resection margin  Multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm are dissected from the attached axilla tail  Section Code  A B  Lateral cavity in relationship to its closest anterior resection margin C  Lateral cavity in relationship to its posterior resection margin  E F  Additional resection of the lateral cavity and its adjacent firm tissue  G H  Representative sections of the medial cavity in relationship to its closest posterior resection margin  I J  Sections the medial cavity in relationship to closest anterior resection margins  K M  Representative sections of the firm tissue surrounding the medial cavity  N O  Representative sections of the grossly unremarkable breast tissue P U  Axillary lymph nodes p 2 lymph nodes q 4 lymph nodes R 2 lymph nodes S    lymph node  representative sections of a 2 5cm nodule  T 3 lymph nodes U 3 lymph nodes Received fresh with the the patient s name and  unit number    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of yellow lobulated fatty tissue and unremarkable tan skin fragments  Sectioning reveals a homogeneous yellow lobulated fatty with a minimal thin white fibrous tissue surface  A discrete mass is not evident  Representative sections are submitted as V Z  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith 