Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 39 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasive carcinoma is present lining the internal aspect of a previously opened cystic mass  Invasive carcinoma is also present in separate fragments of tissue submitted with the main specimen  The margins of resection cannot be accessed  Blood vessels and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The results of estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm irregularly shaped  yellow pink fibromembranous tissue forming the wall of a cystic cavity that was previously opened to reveal an irregular  trabeculated inner lining surface  The wall thickness ranges from REMOVED_DATE   1 0cm  The external surface of the wall is inked black  The internal surface is inked blue for orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue forming the wall of the cyst  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A D  Within the same specimen container are three irregularly shaped  pink yellow soft tissue fragments  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  respectively  Serially sectioning of these soft tissue fragments reveals no gross abnormalities  Representative sections of each fragment are submitted in cassette E  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Andrew H Schulick  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Absent.
