Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 12 29 CLINICAL DATA  Known left breast cancer with DCIS at margins  stitch marks superior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  EXTENSIVE RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  INVOLVING 9 OF 17 BLOCKS  AND PRESENT  0 2 CM FROM THE POSTERIOR AND ANTERIOR MARGINS ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  Note  Ductal carcinoma in situ is extensively present throughout the specimen in the areas adjacent to and distant from the biopsy site  A micropapillary pattern similar to that of the previous specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   is seen within the DCIS  No definite stromal invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 19 05                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a 18 x 12 x 1 2cm simple mastectomy specimen with a skin ellipse of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and a suture on the superior margin  The nipple is unremarkable  There is a linear 3 5cm surgical scar located 2 5cm from the nipple at 1 o clock  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked green and the posterior surface black  Serially sectioning of the posterior margin reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  with a indurated tan brown wall and tan brown soft papillary projections into the cavity  The cavity is surrounded by fat necrosis and fibrous tissue and is directly subjacent to the linear scar on the skin surface  The anterior wall of the biopsy cavity has been previously opened  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm anterior defect  abutting the superior edge of the skin ellipse  The cavity is 0 5cm from the closest posterior margin and 0 6cm deep to the skin  The rest of the margins are  1 0cm from the cavity  Adjacent to  but distinct from the first cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hemorrhagic cavity which contains old blood and fibrin  located at 2 5cm away from the nipple at 5 o clock position  0 2cm from the posterior margin and 0 9cm from anterior margin  This cavity is also surrounded by fat necrosis and fibrous tissue  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fibrofatty without any additional focal lesions  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals 2 papable lymph nodes averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity to the anterior  posterior margins and skin surface  B C  Representative section of the biopsy cavity to the posterior  anterior margins and skin surface  D E  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity to anterior  posterior margins and skin surface  F  A representative section of the biopsy cavity to anterior margin and skin surface  G K  Representative sections of the smaller cavity to the posterior  and anterior margins  L M  Representative sections of breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity from the medial aspect of the specimen  N O  Representative sections of the breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity from the lateral aspect of the specimen  P  Representative sections of the breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity from the superior aspect of the specimen  Q  Representative section of the breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity from the inferior aspect of the specimen  R  Axillary lymph nodes  bisected  S  Representative section of the nipple  Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Isa