imen  which is consistent with the prior biopsy site  The biopsy cavity abuts the anterior margin  is 0 3cm from the posterior margin and is surrounded by tan white fibrous tissue and focal opaque yellow firm adipose tissue consistent with fat necrosis  The remaining breast parenchyma displays unremarkable lobulated tan yellow adipose tissue and dense white to focally yellow fibrous tissue with a few blue domed cysts ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm in greatest dimension  No other discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper outer quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a 19 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm right mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior and a long suture designating the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm disk of tan white skin with a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm centrally located unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue and posterior   black  and is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal mostly dense white to focally yellow fibrous tissue containing multiple blue domed cysts averaging REMOVED_DATE in greatest dimension  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant  Received also are 2 containers  which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  right axillary non sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm irregular portion of tan yellow  lymph  node bearing fat which contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph node  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining fat  Received in formalin  labeled  additional superficial tissue  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm aggregate of multiple irregular portions of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  No masses or lesions are grossly identified  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm strip of tan  wrinkled skin  excised to a depth of 0 5cm  Also in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm triangular portion of tan  wrinkled  hair bearing skin excised to a depth of 0 7cm  Representative sections of both specimens are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast skin   are multiple irregular fragments of gray white skin ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  No masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSES  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT INFRAMAMMARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART B  Lymph Node  Right Intramammary   Sentinel    Excision PART C  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART D  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART E  Lymph Node  Right axilla Non Sentinel   Excision PART F  Breast  Left Superficial Tissue   Exc  report_end  , Present.
