 REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary fat pad  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm area of dense fibrous breast parenchyma containing a 2 0cm area of ill defined retractions  Surrounded by several bright yellow flecks of apparent fat necrosis ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  There is a 1 0cm clot filled cavity at the lesser of the retracting with stellate shaped fibrosis radiating from the center and coming within 0 5cm of the deep  posterior  margin  The area of retraction is underlying the aforementioned skin scar and is located 3 0cm from the nearest  posterior  margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominantly fibrous with focal cystic changes  Several lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm have been dissected from the axillary fat pad  Section code  B H  representative sections of stellate scar and residual biopsy cavity  medial to lateral with skin in G  I J  closest posterior margin K  breast tissue away from biopsy cavity  medial aspect  L  breast tissue away from biopsy cavity  lateral aspect  M W  lymph nodes  single lymph nodes in O  P  Q  Labeled  right breast tissue  are multiple fragments of breast and attached skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm in aggregate  The specimen is sectioned to reveal predominantly fibrous breast parenchyma with focal small cystic changes  No masses are identified  Representative sections are submitted in X GG  Labeled  abdominal flap  is a triangular portion of skin and attached subcutaneous fat measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and excised to a depth of 3 0cm  The skin is grossly unremarkable and the subcutaneous tissue is sectioned to reveal unremarkable adipose tissue  Representative sections of skin and subcutaneous fat are submitted in HH  Labeled  left axillary node  are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate  One fragment is slightly firm and appears to contain a lymph node measuring 0 9cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is entirely submitted in II  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  FIBROFATTY BREAST TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  SONER ALTIOK  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   MAMMOPLASTY PART E  SOFT TISSUE  ABDOMIAL FLAP   EXCISION   report_end  , Present.
