xpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  21 MAY 04 at 15 41     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block B   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER 2 neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 04 at 15 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm portion of fibrofatty tissue with an inserted wire  A short stitch denotes the superior margin and a long stitch the lateral margin  There is blue dye noted between the attached sutures  There appears to be fascia at the deep margin  The anterior margin is marked with blue ink  the posterior margin with black ink  the medial margin with green ink and the lateral margin with yellow ink  The specimen is serially sectioned from the superior to the inferior aspect to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm  tan lesion with irregular borders which extends to 0 1cm from the posterior margin  0 7cm to the lateral margin  0 7cm to the medial margin  1 4cm to the anterior margin  0 8cm to the superior margin and greater than 2 0cm to the inferior margin  The lesion has multiple punctate  soft yellow foci  The remainder of the tissue  approximately 85   consists of adipose tissue with the remaining tissue being soft  white fibrous tissue  The lesion is entirely submitted as A D from the superior to the inferior aspect  Additional sections are submitted as follows  E  Superior end  F  Inferior end  Received in saline   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue  183   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph node  The cut surfaces are soft and tan  The specimen is trisected and entirely submitted as G H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  medial half of cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm unoriented  irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue  with thermal change  On sectioning no masses or nodules are grossly identified  The tissue consists mainly of soft  white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as I and J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  lateral half of cavity   are two unoriented irregular portions of fibrofatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The portions demonstrate thermal artifact  On sectioning no masses or nodules are grossly identified  The tissue is blue dyed stained  The tissue consists of approximately 45  soft  white fibrous tissue  the specimen is entirely submitted as K N  Gross Description by  TIM J  ROBINSON Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT SENTINEL  183  EXCISION PART C  BREAST RIGHT SHAVED MARGIN MEDIAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY  E PART D  BREAST RIGHT SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY   , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of lymphatic vessels  including dermal lymphatics is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 07 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D