are 4 containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME     REMOVED_DATE  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast re excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm piece of breast tissue oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect of the specimen  The long axis of the specimen is oriented from medial to lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  inferior   yellow  A 2 x 1cm defect filled with clotted blood is present on the inferior lateral aspect of the specimen  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white surgical site with a central hemorrhagic area and surrounding fat necrosis  A metallic clip is also present within the surgical site  The site abuts the inferior and lateral aspects of the specimen and is located 1 2cm from the medial margin  0 7cm from the anterior margin  0 6cm from the posterior margin and 0 5cm from the superior margin of the specimen  The remaining parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end margin  radial sections   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Surgical site with closest resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma away from the surgical site  near the medial end of the specimen  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  medial half of cavity   are 2 unoriented and unremarkable pieces of fibroadipose tissue measuring 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The smaller specimen is bisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The larger specimen is bisected and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  lateral half of cavity   are 3 unoriented and grossly unremarkable pieces of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The specimens are entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  low axillary sampling   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  in which 12 lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  are identified  The lymph nodes and the remaining fibroadipose tissue are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes  1 inked black and bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of fibroadipose tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday May 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 08 47 38AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday May 06   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 33 16PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Re excision PART B  Breast  Left  Margin   mediaL half of cavity   Excision PART C  Breast  Left  Margin   lateral half of cavity   Excision PART D  Breast  Left  low axillary sampling   Excision  report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA  Postmenopausal female with a 1 to 2cm round mobile mass in the medial portion of the right breast  No clinical axillary or supraclavicular adenopathy  A recent needle aspiration in office was interpreted as suspicious for carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1 OF 3  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH FEATURES OF NEUROENDOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING FIBROSIS  CYSTS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA WITH FOCAL ATYPICALITY  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No definite lymphatic and vascular invasion is identified  The tumor measures 1 5cm in greatest dimension and is less than 0 1cm from several inked margins  but because of its unusual architectural features  the relative quantities of the invasive and in situ components cannot be adequately assessed  Ductal carcinoma in situ is present at a distance of at least one low power microscopic field from the main tumor mass  Using immunoperoxidase methods on paraffin embedded  formalin fixed tissue  many tumor cells are positive for carcinoembryonic antigen  rare tumor cells are positive for synaptophysin  suggesting neuroendocrine differentiation  and tumor cells are negative for chromogranin  Tumor cells do not show argyrophil granules by the Grimelius method  Dr  Koerner has reviewed this case and agrees with the diagnosis  Unequivocal invasive carcinoma is not identified on the frozen section slide  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN   SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 08     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is an excisional biopsy of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a dark purple  nodular area surrounded by a firm white tissue  The nodule abuts the margin and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  At the periphery is soft  white adipose tissue  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen for ancillary studies  Section Code  A J  nodule and breast biopsy K N  remainder of tissue  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  NO INVASION DEMONSTRATED  O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Rex Neal Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Present.
