 x  6cm biopsy cavity  The biopsy cavity is irregular and focally hemorrhagic and is 0 3cm from the skin margin  0 9cm from the deep margin   the closest margin  and 4 0cm from the lateral margin  The tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity is indurated with focally bright yellow changes and is focally gritty  The remaining parenchyma is composed primarily of dense fibroadipose tissue  There is a 14 x 7 x 2 5cm portion of attached axillary tail which is sectioned to reveal multiple  8  lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest skin margin  B  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest deep margin  C D  Representative sections of gritty biopsy cavity  E  Biopsy cavity in relation to adjacent fibrous tissue  F  Biopsy cavity in relation to inverted nipple  G I  Representative sections of lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left additional axillary contents  are two fragmented gray lymph nodes each with a small amount of attached adipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Each is bisected and entirely submitted in cassettes J and K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 19 x 15 x 3cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior margin and a long suture designating the anatomical lateral margin  patient is status post right axillary dissection   There is an overlying central 15 x 5cm tan skin ellipse with a central unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is a curvilinear 2 5cm in length well healed scar which is 0 7cm inferomedial to the nipple  There is a second 2 5cm linear well healed  focally puckered scar  1 2cm superomedially from the areola complex and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm wrinkled  focally nodular scar 0 9cm from the long suture  lateral margin  and 3cm superomedially from the areola complex  A REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm dark brown macule abuts one skin margin at the inferior aspect  Sectioning beneath the linear  puckered superomedial scar reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm predominantly smooth  gray pink biopsy cavity which comes within 0 1cm of the closest deep margin  The biopsy cavity comes to within 0 8cm of the overlying scar and 1 0cm from the superior margin  The tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity is focally indurated with diffuse bright yellow changes in the parenchyma  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm smooth lined cystic area located 0 9cm below the healed curvilinear scar  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan  diffusely granular firm area of fibrous tissue 3cm from the lateral margin  the closest margin   Additionally  there are two firm  ill  defined nodules each averaging 0 6cm in greatest dimension which come within 1 5cm of the lateral margin  SECTION CODE L  Biopsy cavity beneath puckered scar in relation to closest deep margin  M  Biopsy cavity in relation to puckered scar  N O  Biopsy cavity beneath puckered scar with adjacent indurated yellow parenchyma  P  Biopsy cavity beneath puckered scar in relation to adjacent firm fibrous tissue  Q R  Second well healed cystic biopsy cavity beneath curvilinear scar submitted in its entirety  S  Representative section of firm  granular focus in the lateral portion  T  Nodule from lateral area  U  Macule from skin ellipse  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael V Seiden  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Absent.
