ficial soft tissue margins  Multiple REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm satellite nodules are present in the specimen and one 0 4cm tan nodule abuts the inferior deep inked margin  However  the medial and lateral resectiion margins are greater than 2cm from gross tumor  The axillary tail contains multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm  All the lymph nodes are white and rubbery  Section Code A B   nipple and tumor C D   representative ulcer E F   firm skin adjacent to nipple G   scar H K   representative tumor L M   superior superficial margin  radial sections N   inferior superficial  radial margin O   medial  en face margin P   lateral  en face margin Q   deep radial margin R U   lymph nodes EE FF   deep margin  radial section GG   deep inferior margin  radial section Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are multiple parts  Labeled  superior margin left breast  is a tissue fragment  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  soft  yellow tan  submitted entirely as frozen  1 in V  Labeled  inferior margin left breast  is a fragment of soft  yellow tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  entirely frozen as frozen  2 and submitted in W  Labeled  new superior margin  is a 16cm long and 0 9cm wide skin ellipse excised to a depth of 1 4cm  A stitch designates the opposite surface to the new superior margin  The new margin is inked and representative  non stitch  margin is frozen as frozen  3  5  in X to Z respectively  Additional unfrozen new superior margin from the peripheral ends of the skin ellipse are submitted in AA and BB  Labeled  superior margin  3  left breast  and  suture on inferior margin  is a 7 x 0 9cm wide skin ellipse excised to a depth of 1 4cm with a suture in place on the inferior margin  The skin ellipse is unremarkable  Representative new superior margin is taken from the central portion of the ellipse and frozen as frozen  6 in CC  The remainder of this newest superior margin is e