la at the opposite end of the skin ellipse  In the center of the areola with a 1 0cm in diameter unremarkable nipple 0 5cm inferior to the nipple is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm apparent acrochordon on the areola  1 7cm from the areolar margin  Also received in the same container is a separate 15 x 4 5cm skin ellipse  with 2cm of underlying adipose tissue  Both the skin and the adipose tissue are unremarkable  The mastectomy specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of fibrous tissue beneath the scar  The fibrous tissue beneath the scar extends to 3 5cm from the deep resection margin and 3 0cm from the closest lateral resection margin  Within the remainder of the breast parenchyma are focal areas of rubbery tan breast parechyma  No firm  stellate  or gritty area are identified  SECTION CODE  A  skin with scar B  nipple C  acrochordon on areola D G  sections of biopsy site with inked margins H M  additional sections of breast parenchyma distant from biopsy site N U  lymph nodes from axillary tale V  representative section of separate skin ellipse  Resident  Jeoffry Brennick  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  David Bent Smith  M D  James M Fitzgerald  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLA   report_end  , Absent.
